    "problem_statement": "CachingMiddleware cache not flushing at expected threshold\n\n#### Description\n\nThe CachingMiddleware is not flushing the cache when it reaches the WRITE_CACHE_SIZE threshold. After performing multiple write operations that should trigger a cache flush, the cache remains empty when it should contain data.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom tinydb import TinyDB\nfrom tinydb.middlewares import CachingMiddleware\nfrom tinydb.storages import MemoryStorage\n\n# Create a database with caching middleware\nstorage = CachingMiddleware(MemoryStorage())\ndb = TinyDB(storage=storage)\n\n# Write documents up to the cache size threshold\ndoc = {'test': 'data'}\nfor _ in range(CachingMiddleware.WRITE_CACHE_SIZE - 1):\n    storage.write(doc)\n\nprint(f\"Cache after {CachingMiddleware.WRITE_CACHE_SIZE - 1} writes:\", storage.memory)\n# Expected: None (cache not yet flushed)\n\n# Write one more document to reach the threshold\nstorage.write(doc)\nprint(f\"Cache after {CachingMiddleware.WRITE_CACHE_SIZE} writes:\", storage.memory)\n# Expected: should contain data (cache should be flushed and populated)\n# Actual: None\n```\n\nThe cache should flush and be populated with data when reaching the WRITE_CACHE_SIZE threshold, but it remains None instead."
  },
